# J14 — Narrow terminal (responsive matrix)
# Re-run the J1 walk at 60x20. Exercises adaptive-footer wrap (<70 cols) and
# compact-Workbench collapse. For the 80x24 cell of the matrix, re-run:
#   ./scripts/devex/run-journey.sh --size 80x24 J14
name: Narrow terminal (60x20)
size: 60x20
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch:
wait-for: 2 CHOOSE A TARGET
snap: narrow-target-gate
expect: Enter selects
ask: 60 cols — is the target gate readable, does the footer wrap to two lines instead of truncating behind a +more chip?
keys: Enter
wait-for: 3 CHOOSE A MODEL
snap: narrow-model-gate
expect: Target confirmed
keys: Down Down Down Enter
wait-for: 5 CHOOSE AUTH METHOD
snap: narrow-credentials-gate
expect: Target confirmed
expect: API key (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)
type: bdd-session-only-key
keys: Enter
wait-for: 10 KUMI-KATA
snap: narrow-planning-gate
expect: Target confirmed
expect: Focused: Gather repo context
expect: Enter:
expect: Space check
expect: Enter run
expect-not: tool descriptor missing
ask: Planning at 60x20 — are the selected tasks, exact Enter outcome, and controls all visible without internal or mid-word cropping?
keys: Down
wait: 0.1
keys: Down
wait: 0.1
keys: Down
wait: 0.1
keys: Down
wait: 0.1
keys: Down
wait: 0.1
keys: Down
wait: 0.5
snap: narrow-planning-scrolled
expect: TASKS
expect: > SKIP    Threat intel (CVEs)
expect: Enter:
expect: Enter run
ask: Scrolled Planning — did the task window follow the cursor while keeping the confirmation and controls fixed?
keys: Escape
submit: demo
wait-for: 90 run completed
snap: narrow-demo-result
ask: Compact Workbench/Activity — do findings and detail text stay readable, with nothing truncated behind chrome?
submit: findings
wait: 3
snap: narrow-findings
ask: Findings at 60x20 — severity/confidence signifiers still visible per row, or clipped?
